#
# Conformance case: teleology/iteration-combinator.
#
# A logic:Iteration program combinator (loop operator) is declared with a loop
# body (retryAction) and a loop condition (resourceStillAvailable). The body is
# repeated while the condition holds; when it does not, the iteration terminates.
# This pins the structural vocabulary: logic:iterationBody and
# logic:iterationCondition are the two dedicated properties of logic:Iteration
# (binary left/right operands do not fit a loop — a body and a condition are not
# co-equal operands). The case also demonstrates the connection to
# logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess quantification: a strong-cyclic plan succeeds
# when every fair execution of such a loop terminates at the goal in finitely
# many steps.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live
# in input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/iteration-combinator/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
